# http headers for llm discovery
# this is for llms not humans
#
# headless ai fetchers (claude code, cursor, future chatgpt browse) read the
# Link response header and skip the html body. json-ld doesnt reach them, only
# wire-level signals do
#
# activates on hosts that support the _headers format. the html <link> tag and
# the .md endpoints remain the portable discovery fallback.
#
# .md endpoints are emitted by src/pages/[...path].md.ts

# default security and cache policy. Link and Vary do not belong here: applying
# them to every font, image, and script needlessly fragments caches and bloats
# asset responses. page-specific Link headers are below, while runtime content
# negotiation adds Vary: Accept only to URLs that can actually vary.
# HSTS is intentionally a
# conservative 6 months without preload until we've verified https only on
# every subdomain - once verified, bump max-age to 31536000 and add preload.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=(), browsing-topics=()

# per-route Link header pointing at the matching .md
# matching rules combine, so the security/cache default and the per-route rule
# both fire on the same request

